cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Walkfigure
message: >-
  If you use Walkfigure in work you publish, please cite it as below. Please also cite Sports2D, whose pose stage
  Walkfigure's engine is built from, and Lencioni et al. for the typical-walking reference curves.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chnani
    given-names: Moh
    affiliation: MGAM LLC
abstract: >-
  Walkfigure measures the sagittal-plane joint angles and the timing and spacing of a person's steps from a single video
  recorded with an ordinary camera, and shows the walk as a three-dimensional figure that can be turned, stepped through
  frame by frame, and compared with a typical walker built from published reference curves. It measures hip, knee, ankle
  and trunk angles, heel strikes and toe-offs, cadence, stride time, stance and double support, step length, toe
  clearance and heel rise, with per-stride variability and left-to-right symmetry. The analysis runs entirely on the
  user's own computer; no video or result is uploaded. Walkfigure is research software and is not a medical device: it
  does not diagnose, it does not recommend treatment, and its numbers are estimates to be checked against the recording.
version: 1.1.66
date-released: '2026-09-18'
url: https://mgam.bio/walkfigure
repository-artifact: https://github.com/mgambio/walkfigure/releases
license-url: https://github.com/mgambio/walkfigure/blob/master/LICENCE.txt
keywords:
  - gait analysis
  - markerless motion capture
  - pose estimation
  - biomechanics
  - rehabilitation
  - kinematics
references:
